AltoLeverageSwapperMultiTarget::swap(address,address,uint256,bytes)
├── given caller is not whitelisted including the owner
│   └── it should revert with AltoLeverageSwapperSenderNotValid before decoding parameters and preserve balances and target allowance
└── given caller is whitelisted
    ├── when encoded swap parameters are malformed
    │   └── it should revert with empty ABI decoding error data and preserve balances and target allowance
    ├── when selected target is zero unlisted or revoked
    │   └── it should revert with AltoLeverageSwapperInvalidSwapTarget before pulling tokens and preserve balances and target allowance
    ├── given swap parameters and selected target are valid
    │   ├── when the caller allowance is insufficient
    │   │   └── it should bubble ERC20InsufficientAllowance and preserve balances and target allowance
    │   ├── when the caller balance is insufficient
    │   │   └── it should bubble ERC20InsufficientBalance and preserve balances and target allowance
    │   ├── when transferFrom returns false
    │   │   └── it should revert with SafeERC20FailedOperation and preserve balances and target allowance
    │   ├── when the target attempts to spend more than amountIn and its call fails
    │   │   └── it should replace the target error with AltoLeverageSwapperSwapFailed and roll back transfers and approvals
    │   ├── when received output is one wei below minAmountOut
    │   │   └── it should revert with AltoLeverageSwapperMinAmountOutNotMet containing both exact amounts and roll back the swap
    │   ├── when clearing the target approval returns false
    │   │   └── it should revert with SafeERC20FailedOperation and roll back the swap and approvals
    │   ├── when transferring the leftover sell tokens returns false
    │   │   └── it should revert with SafeERC20FailedOperation and roll back the swap and approvals
    │   ├── when transferring the bought tokens returns false
    │   │   └── it should revert with SafeERC20FailedOperation and roll back the swap and approvals
    │   └── when sellToken equals buyToken and the swap reduces the token balance
    │       └── it should revert with arithmetic panic 0x11 during balance subtraction and roll back the swap
    └── given sellToken and buyToken are distinct and the swap completes
        ├── when all input is spent and received output equals the minimum
        │   └── it should accept equality and transfer the bought tokens without a sell refund
        ├── when input is partially spent and output exceeds the minimum
        │   └── it should return the unspent portion and transfer the bought tokens
        ├── when no input is spent and output and minimum are zero
        │   └── it should refund all input without transferring bought tokens
        ├── when amountIn is zero
        │   └── it should accept a zero input and zero output swap
        ├── when the target returns a large amount without transferring output
        │   └── it should ignore the returned value and use the actual zero balance delta
        ├── when native value is attached
        │   └── it should retain that value in the swapper without forwarding it to the target
        ├── when the valid selected target has no code and minimum is zero
        │   └── it should accept the successful no-op call and refund the input
        ├── when another valid target is selected
        │   └── it should use only the selected target and leave the original target balances and allowance unchanged
        ├── it should preserve preexisting sell and buy token balances on the swapper
        ├── it should clear the target allowance after execution
        ├── it should return the exact bought-token balance delta
        └── it should emit Swap with target token addresses input output and leftover amounts exactly
